    "_postman_id": "84fb493b-e285-4151-b6dd-5c2414089332",
    "name": "sarahaa",
    "description": "# Sarahaa API (Anonymous Messages)\n\nThis collection documents a simple **anonymous messaging** API (similar to “Sarahah”). It contains endpoints for:\n\n- **Auth**: signup, login, confirm email\n    \n- **User**: view profile, share profile, update profile, freeze account, update password\n    \n- **Message**: send anonymous message, delete message\n    \n\n> **Environment / variables** \n  \n\n## Base URL\n\nThis collection is configured to use the variable:\n\n- `{{onlone-url}}` → `http://saraha-anonymous-message.eu-4.evennode.com/`\n    \n\nSome requests still point to `http://localhost:3000/...` (local dev). To make the collection consistent, consider replacing those URLs with `{{onlone-url}}` as well.\n\n## Common variables\n\nThe collection currently has these collection variables (as saved in the collection):\n\n- `{{onlone-url}}` (base URL)\n    \n- `{{token}}` (a Bearer token string)\n    \n- `{{bearer}}`, `{{bearer1}}` (raw JWTs)\n    \n\n> Recommendation: standardize on **one** variable, e.g. `{{accessToken}}`, and use it consistently via the header `Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}`. \n  \n\n---\n\n# Authentication\n\nMost “user” endpoints require a JWT access token.\n\n## Header\n\nUse the `Authorization` header:\n\n``` http\nAuthorization: Bearer <jwt>\n\n ```\n\nNotes based on existing saved requests:\n\n- Some requests use `Authorization` (capital A), others `authorization`.\n    \n- Some requests include a raw token without the `Bearer` prefix.\n    \n\n> Recommendation: keep it consistent with `Authorization: Bearer {{token}}`. \n  \n\n---\n\n# Content Types\n\nWhen sending JSON payloads, use:\n\n``` http\nContent-Type: application/json\n\n ```\n\n(Several requests have JSON bodies saved but no explicit `Content-Type` header. Many servers still accept it, but documenting it is helpful.)\n\n---\n\n# Error format (expected)\n\nNo error examples are saved in this collection. A typical error response pattern for REST APIs is:\n\n``` json\n{\n  \"message\": \"<human-readable error>\",\n  \"errors\": [\n    {\n      \"field\": \"<field>\",\n      \"message\": \"<field error>\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n\n ```\n\nCommon HTTP status codes you may see:\n\n- `400` Validation error / bad request\n    \n- `401` Missing/invalid token\n    \n- `403` Not allowed\n    \n- `404` Not found\n    \n- `409` Conflict (duplicate email/username)\n    \n- `500` Server error\n    \n\n---\n\n# How to use this collection\n\n1. **Signup** a new user.\n    \n2. **Confirm email** (requires a confirmation token).\n    \n3. **Login** to receive an access token.\n    \n4. Use the token for any **protected user** endpoints.\n    \n5. Use **Share profile** to get a `userId`, then use **Send message** to send anonymous messages to that user.\n    \n\n---\n\n# Notes / gaps\n\n- This collection currently has **no saved examples** (responses). To enable richer documentation and to support mocking, save at least one example per request after sending real requests.\n    \n- Some endpoints appear duplicated between `localhost` and `{{onlone-url}}`. Consider standardizing to one base URL.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json",
    "_exporter_id": "32886557"
  },
